      "finalPromptText": "[Sat 2026-07-25 00:22 CDT] You are taking a bounded, recorded math exam for Cortex Learning OS.\n\nAnswer independently without tools. Return only valid JSON with shape {\"answers\":[{\"itemId\":\"...\",\"answer\":\"...\"}]}.\n\nGive exactly one answer for every item. Do not include reasoning, markdown, commentary, or confidence.\n\nNo learning context is supplied for this baseline run.\n\nExam title: Math Foundations Baseline v0\n\nItems:\n[{\"itemId\":\"mf-01\",\"prompt\":\"Solve (3/4)x - 5/6 = 7/3. Give x as a fraction or decimal.\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-02\",\"prompt\":\"Give the real solution set of x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0 as comma-separated values.\",\"answerFormat\":\"set\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-03\",\"prompt\":\"Let f(x)=x^2-3x+1. Compute 2f(-1)-f(2).\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-04\",\"prompt\":\"For f(x)=3x-7, compute f^{-1}(11).\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-05\",\"prompt\":\"Compute the infinite sum 3 + 1.5 + 0.75 + ... .\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-06\",\"prompt\":\"Give the solution set of |2x-3|=7 as comma-separated values.\",\"answerFormat\":\"set\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-07\",\"prompt\":\"A fair coin is tossed 4 times. What is the probability of exactly 2 heads?\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-08\",\"prompt\":\"A fair six-sided die is rolled 3 times. What is the probability of at least one 6?\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-09\",\"prompt\":\"A condition has 1% prevalence. A test has 99% sensitivity and 95% specificity. Given a positive test, what is the probability of the condition?\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-10\",\"prompt\":\"Independent events have P(A)=0.4 and P(B)=0.5. Compute P(A union B).\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-11\",\"prompt\":\"For X~Bernoulli(0.3), compute Var(X).\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-12\",\"prompt\":\"Compute the arithmetic mean of 4, 7, 9, 10.\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-13\",\"prompt\":\"A score of 80 has weight 0.25 and 92 has weight 0.75. Compute the weighted mean.\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-14\",\"prompt\":\"Compute the median of 2, 4, 4, 9, 100.\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-15\",\"prompt\":\"An observation is 85, the mean is 70, and the standard deviation is 5. Compute its z-score.\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-16\",\"prompt\":\"For f(x)=x^3-6x^2+9x, compute f'(2).\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-17\",\"prompt\":\"What is the minimum value of x^2-8x+20 over real x?\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-18\",\"prompt\":\"Give the minimizing point (x,y) for x^2+y^2-6x+4y as comma-separated values.\",\"answerFormat\":\"set\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-19\",\"prompt\":\"A quantity rises from 80 to 100. What is the percent increase? Give a decimal probability or percentage number without the % sign.\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-20\",\"prompt\":\"A game pays +10 with probability 0.2 and -3 with probability 0.8. Compute expected payoff.\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-21\",\"prompt\":\"Given P(A and B)=0.18 and P(B)=0.3, compute P(A|B).\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-22\",\"prompt\":\"For independent fair coin tosses, what is the expected number of tosses until the pattern HT first appears?\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-23\",\"prompt\":\"Two fair dice are rolled. Given that at least one die is a 6, what is the probability both dice are 6?\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-24\",\"prompt\":\"Two cards are drawn uniformly without replacement from a standard 52-card deck. Probability both are aces?\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-25\",\"prompt\":\"In the standard Monty Hall setup, you initially choose one of 3 doors, the host knows the prize location and always opens a different losing door. What is the probability of winning if you switch?\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-26\",\"prompt\":\"A random variable has mean 0 and variance 4. Compute E[X^2].\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-27\",\"prompt\":\"A rectangle has perimeter 20. What is its maximum possible area?\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-28\",\"prompt\":\"Compute det([[2,1,0],[1,3,1],[0,2,4]]).\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-29\",\"prompt\":\"In a population, P(A)=0.5, P(B)=0.4, P(C)=0.3; pairwise intersections are 0.2, 0.15, 0.1; and P(A and B and C)=0.05. Compute P(A union B union C).\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"},{\"itemId\":\"mf-30\",\"prompt\":\"Two fair six-sided dice are rolled. Compute the expected value of the maximum of the two dice.\",\"answerFormat\":\"number\"}]\n\n[Bootstrap truncation warning]\nSome workspace bootstrap files were truncated before injection.\nTreat Project Context as partial and read the relevant files directly if details seem missing.\n- AGENTS.md: 25944 raw -> 11999 injected (~54% removed; max/file).\n- TOOLS.md: 14771 raw -> 11999 injected (~19% removed; max/file).\n- MEMORY.md: 12729 raw -> 11999 injected (~6% removed; max/file).\n- If unintentional, raise agents.defaults.bootstrapMaxChars and/or agents.defaults.bootstrapTotalMaxChars.",
